course: dictionary
lesson: 13676
title: Breathing words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inhalation is a noun. It is the act of breathing air, smoke or medicine into your lungs. Look for the clues around it: «Take a slow, deep inhalation, then breathe out.» Breathing out is the opposite, so inhalation must mean breathing in.
explain: The word is about the lungs. When you take an inhalation, your chest gets bigger as air rushes in. In science you learn that the diaphragm, a muscle under your lungs, moves down when you inhale.
explain: The word also appears in health and safety. «Smoke inhalation is the biggest danger in a house fire.» Here the clues are smoke and fire, so smoke inhalation means breathing in smoke, which is harmful. «Her inhaler gives her medicine by inhalation» shows that medicine can also reach your lungs this way.
fact: Inhalation means breathing in air, smoke or medicine into your lungs.
fact: Exhalation is the opposite: breathing out.
fact: The diaphragm moves down when you inhale.
fact: «Smoke inhalation» means breathing in smoke, and it is the main danger in fires.
fact: An inhaler gives medicine by inhalation, so the medicine goes straight into the lungs.
exercise: «Take a slow, deep inhalation, then breathe out.» What does inhalation mean? | Breathing out | *Breathing in | Shouting loudly | Holding your nose
exercise: «Smoke inhalation is the biggest danger in a house fire.» What is the danger? | *Breathing in smoke | Getting wet from the rain | Being too cold | Hearing loud alarms
exercise: «Her inhaler gives her medicine by inhalation.» How does the medicine get into her body? | *By breathing it in | By swallowing it whole | By drinking it with water | By rubbing it on her skin
test: What is the opposite of inhalation? | *Exhalation | Diaphragm | Inhalation | Medicine
test: «The doctor asked him for a deep inhalation.» What did the doctor ask him to do? | *Breathe in deeply | Sit down quickly | Lie still and close his eyes | Run around the room
exam: In a science lesson, the teacher says, «When you inhale, your diaphragm moves down.» What does inhale mean? | Cough loudly | *Breathe in | Stand up tall | Breathe out
